.TH PATH_COLLAPSE 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
path_collapse \- Collapse redundant separators and "." entries in a path

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/path_internal.h>
.IB #include <lib/byte.h>

.IB size_t
.IB path_collapse(char* path, size_t n);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBpath_collapse\fR function collapses redundant separators and "." entries in a given path. It modifies the input path in place.

.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.IB path
The input path string to be collapsed.
.TP
.IB n
The length of the input path string.

.SH RETURN VALUE
The function returns the length of the collapsed path.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBpath_collapse\fR function:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/path_internal.h>
#include <lib/byte.h>

int main() {
    char path[] = "/usr//lib/../lib";
    size_t len = strlen(path);
    len = path_collapse(path, len);
    printf("Collapsed path: %.*s\n", (int)len, path);
    return 0;
}
.nef